Seniority level

Mid-Senior level

Employment type

Full-time

Job function

Information Technology

Industries

Transportation, Logistics, Supply Chain and Storage and IT Services and IT Consulting

About The Role

We are looking for a Data Analyst to join our team. You'll be conducting analytics on our pricing operations to ensure we provide our customers with competitive and fair pricing. This is a great opportunity to learn more about the Australian Energy market and state-of-the-art data infrastructure, together with our team of Australian Energy market experts and data experts.

What You'll Do

Provide our Pricing & Sales Team with insights into our electricity and gas pricing strategy, using historical consumption, price and customer pricing data;
Support our revenue assurance track, making sure that we are billed correctly by other market participants;
Support Sales forecasting by creating an estimation of our future sales;
Work closely with our Data Engineering team, making sure that you have the right data available;
Work collaboratively with business units to ensure developed reports and data are clear, functional, and effective in communicating messages and insights using suitable data visualisation techniques and methods;
Write data models in dbt using SQL;
Write python scripts to support the pricing analysis;
Create reports and dashboards using Holistics;

You Will Be a Good Candidate If You

Have completed relevant education, a relevant (energy) technical/finance education is a strong advantage;
Have a proven track record of 1-3 years of experience working as an analyst;
Are skillful in SQL, python and Excel;
Have excellent communication skills, an eye for detail, and work accurately;
Are able to work independently and don’t mind being an all-rounder;
Have strong analytical and problem solving skills;
Have good stakeholder management, communication skills and a proven track record of meeting deadlines.

Extra Points If You

Have experience with responding to notices to provide information to energy market regulators and commissions and have a passion for renewable energy;
Have experience with reporting requirements of regulators or government bodies;
Are familiar with Git, Dagster, Snowflake or Salesforce;
Are familiar with data visualisations tools, such as Tableau or PowerBI.

Culture & Benefits

A challenging start-up position where you can make an impact;
Get involved in our regional expansion from the ground up to chart the future of Flo;
A lot of freedom and an essential role;
Work in an open-minded and dynamic environment with a talented team;
Enjoy an attractive compensation package (with attractive variable components), generous time-off and a great work-life balance.

About Flo Energy

Hi, we are Flo! We are on a mission to switch as many people and businesses as possible to affordable, renewable solutions.

We began in a small shophouse in Singapore and have grown rapidly ever since, expanding into Australia with even bigger plans ahead.

Unlike other retailers, we have built our own best-in-class energy platform entirely in-house. Designed specifically for the sector, it automates complex processes and keeps costs down, letting us offer genuinely affordable products to our customers.

Behind Flo is a diverse team of passionate engineers, data scientists, operators, and energy experts. We come from different backgrounds, but we are united by the shared goal of creating a more sustainable future. If you want to make an impact and help accelerate the renewable energy transition, we would love to meet you.

Find out more about us on https://floenergy.sg/business

